        # substituted into it. That is the only boundary the box faces of a hard
        # CSG have: their silhouettes are globally excluded, so without this the
        # face edges are handed whole to the subpixel walk, which cannot pin
        # them — near a face's own edge the two ray roots pinch together and stay
        # ambiguous at every cell size, scale independently.
